title: 'Move on-demand coretime orders to the Coretime chain'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `pallet-on-demand`, which is the first step of moving the on-demand
    coretime purchase functionality to the Coretime chain.

    The Relay chain still owns the real on-demand order queue, so this pallet acts
    as a front-end for it. The spot price of on-demand coretime is based on a
    local estimate of the queue depth. The real queue is not used, because it is
    one hop away, and because it will be moved to the Coretime chain in the future
    anyway. The estimate is increased with every accepted order and decreased at a
    constant rate per Relay Chain block, per pool core. The details of the
    price computation are delegated to an implementation of the `PricingProvider`
    trait, with a default implementation provided which raises the price
    exponentially with the queue depth, starting at a configured base fee and
    raising it by a predefined percentage for each outstanding order in the
    estimated queue. Orders are rejected if the number of outstanding orders
    reaches a configured maximum value, or when the on-demand pool has no cores
    assigned.

    `place_order` charges the caller the spot price into the pallet's own pot
    account, as long as it doesn't exceed a maximum acceptable price defined by the
    caller. An accepted order is appended to a pending batch, and the whole batch is
    sent to the Relay Chain on finalization of the block.

    On the Relay Chain side, the existing on-demand pallet gains the receiving end:
    a new `queue_on_demand_batch` call, callable only by the Coretime chain or root,
    which pushes the whole batch into the on-demand order queue.
crates:
- name: pallet-on-demand
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: minor
